<https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/morphoeval-delphi10000-ceratites-nodosus-turing-wavelength-s0-code-traceability> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Ceratites nodosus Schnakenberg Turing wavenumber at 26 µm (Ladinian, 240 Ma) — Code-to-model traceability: 80/100" ;
    dct:date "2026-10-27"^^xsd:date ;
    dct:description "The module docstring and the diffusivity solver name the Turing wavenumber. Lean theorems check the integer wavelength counts (1250, and 42 per organ-scale rib) and the sign of the integer Turing numerator. They are not a real-analysis proof of the dispersion relation." ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/concept/morphoeval-0.1.0-code-traceability> ;
    pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/model/grok-4.7> ;
    pk:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/code-traceability" ;
    pk:hasEvidence <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/morphoeval-delphi10000-ceratites-nodosus-turing-wavelength-s0-code-traceability-1>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/morphoeval-delphi10000-ceratites-nodosus-turing-wavelength-s0-code-traceability-2> ;
    pk:hasScore 8e-01 ;
    pk:hasVerdict "faithful" .

<https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/morphoeval-delphi10000-ceratites-nodosus-turing-wavelength-s0-model-fidelity> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Ceratites nodosus Schnakenberg Turing wavenumber at 26 µm (Ladinian, 240 Ma) — Model fidelity to source: 84/100" ;
    dct:date "2026-10-27"^^xsd:date ;
    dct:description "The script linearises Schnakenberg kinetics, sets k_c^2 = sqrt(det J / (Du Dv)), and integrates the nonlinear PDE on a periodic patch. Operating Du is solved for 26 µm rather than copied from the 1.1 mm sibling. The one-step Euler dispersion test uses a large diffusive timestep, so stiff modes miss the continuous curve (RMSE 0.50)." ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/concept/morphoeval-0.1.0-model-fidelity> ;
    pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/model/grok-4.7> ;
    pk:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/model-fidelity" ;
    pk:hasEvidence <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/morphoeval-delphi10000-ceratites-nodosus-turing-wavelength-s0-model-fidelity-1>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/morphoeval-delphi10000-ceratites-nodosus-turing-wavelength-s0-model-fidelity-2> ;
    pk:hasScore 8.4e-01 ;
    pk:hasVerdict "faithful" .

<https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/morphoeval-delphi10000-ceratites-nodosus-turing-wavelength-s0-morphometric-validation> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Ceratites nodosus Schnakenberg Turing wavenumber at 26 µm (Ladinian, 240 Ma) — Morphometric validation: 82/100" ;
    dct:date "2026-10-27"^^xsd:date ;
    dct:description "Full-curve Pearson r is 0.990 and the radial FFT peak is exactly 2.56e-05 m. Specimen circularity is 0.659 against a circle null of 1, foreground fraction 0.505 against 0.70, coherency 0.522 against 0.25. Radial KS versus the photograph is 0.94, which is the expected mismatch at a scale the photo cannot resolve. Unstable-band r is only 0.964." ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/concept/morphoeval-0.1.0-morphometric-validation> ;
    pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/model/grok-4.7> ;
    pk:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/morphometric-validation" ;
